OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ARise in babies in care proceedings
OL,4,Araises fears of unnecessary adoptions,
OL,5,Aexperts tell BBC
OL,6,
OL,7,FWhile there are cases where it is
OL,8,Funsafe for parents to continue contact
OL,9,Fwith their children, experts have told
OL,10,FFile on 4 Investigates that many babies
OL,11,Fmay not have needed to go into care if
OL,12,Fsupport had been in place.
OL,14,FAnd, since very young children who go
OL,15,Finto care are more likely to be adopted
OL,16,Fthan older children, there are also
OL,17,Fconcerns from experts that some may
OL,18,Fhave been permanently separated from
OL,19,Ftheir birth families unnecessarily.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
